# check: run
# QCB: refused while scopes were written; inferred, each value is built where it is kept (O28), and the
# program runs - read after what it was built in closes, as the description below says it would be
# B11, E25: a value local a call given a scope argument declares lives where the argument says (the fifth any review,
# 5) - so the note names the scope argument to change, never a declaration (study 4's r05 had it the other way, when
# such a local's storage was its block)
# (a function of its own: filepath.Join is variadic since D8g, its arguments then held in the caller's frame)
fn glue(a String&, b String&) String { return $a "/" $b }
fn joined(dir String&, names Array<String&>&, out mut Vec<String&>&) {
    for name in names {
        p := glue(dir, name)
        out.Push(p)
    }
}
fn main() ? {
    l := Vec<String&>()
    joined("d", Array<String&>["a", "b"], l)
}
